# Environment Configuration

## Environment Variables
- **API URL**: `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` - Backend API base URL
- **Never hardcode**: IP addresses or localhost values
- **All config**: Managed via environment files (.env.local, .env.production)

## Environment Files
- `.env.local` - Local development
- `.env.production` - Production
- `.env.example` - Template (if exists)

## Configuration Pattern
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Use environment variables
const API_BASE_URL = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL || 'http://localhost:4001';

// ❌ WRONG: Hardcoded values
const API_BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:4001';
const API_BASE_URL = 'http://192.168.1.100:4001';
```

## API Configuration
- Base URL from `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`
- API version: `/api`
- Full URL: `${API_BASE_URL}${API_VERSION}`
- Defined in [src/lib/api.ts](mdc:src/lib/api.ts)

## Client-Side Variables
- Use `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix for client-side variables
- Access via `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_*`
- Available at build time
- Don't expose sensitive data

## Server-Side Variables
- No `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix
- Access in API routes only
- Not exposed to client
- Use for sensitive data

## Configuration Management
- Store in `.env.local` for development
- Use Vercel environment variables for production
- Never commit `.env.local` to git
- Document required variables in README

## Common Variables
```bash
# API Configuration
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4001

# Feature Flags (if needed)
NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_FEATURE_X=true

# Analytics (if needed)
NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_ID=xxx
```

## Best Practices
- ✅ Use environment variables for all configuration
- ✅ Provide sensible defaults
- ✅ Document required variables
- ✅ Use different values per environment
- ❌ Never hardcode URLs or IPs
- ❌ Never commit secrets
- ❌ Never expose server-side variables to client
